{"step_index":545,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T16:19:39Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-19T21:49:39+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-19T21:49:39+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/win-10/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/neurax_app/modules/defect_detector.py`\nTotal Lines: 375\nTotal Bytes: 13992\nShowing lines 320 to 375\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n320: \n321: def annotate_boxes_hud(img: Image.Image, detections: list[dict], status: str) -> Image.Image:\n322:     \"\"\"Draws bounding boxes around localized defect regions.\"\"\"\n323:     w, h = img.size\n324:     overlay = Image.new('RGBA', (w, h), (0, 0, 0, 0))\n325:     draw_overlay = ImageDraw.Draw(overlay)\n326:     draw = ImageDraw.Draw(img)\n327: \n328:     for det in detections:\n329:         bbox = det.get('bbox')\n330:         dtype = det['defect_type'].lower()\n331:         if bbox is None or dtype in ('normal', 'acceptable', 'pass'):\n332:             continue\n333: \n334:         x1, y1, x2, y2 = [int(v) for v in bbox]\n335:         color_hex = DEFECT_COLORS.get(dtype, '#e74c3c')\n336:         c_rgb = tuple(int(color_hex.lstrip('#')[i:i+2], 16) for i in (0, 2, 4))\n337:         \n338:         draw_overlay.rectangle([x1, y1, x2, y2], fill=c_rgb + (40,))\n339:         box_thickness = max(2, int(min(w, h) / 200))\n340:         draw.rectangle([x1, y1, x2, y2], outline=color_hex, width=box_thickness)\n341: \n342:         # Tag\n343:         label = f\" {dtype.upper()} {det['confidence']*100:.0f}% \"\n344:         try:\n345:             font = ImageFont.truetype(\"arialbd.ttf\", max(10, int(min(w, h) / 50)))\n346:         except Exception:\n347:             font = ImageFont.load_default()\n348: \n349:         lbl_y1 = max(0, y1 - 18)\n350:         draw.rectangle([x1, lbl_y1, x1 + len(label)*7, y1], fill=color_hex)\n351:         draw.text((x1 + 2, lbl_y1 + 1), label, fill='white', font=font)\n352: \n353:     return Image.alpha_composite(img.convert('RGBA'), overlay).convert('RGB')\n354: \n355: \n356: # ── Heatmap Overlay ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n357: \n358: def generate_heatmap_overlay(\n359:     img: Image.Image,\n360:     cam: np.ndarray | None,\n361:     status: str,\n362:     defect_type: str,\n363: ) -> Image.Image:\n364:     \"\"\"Creates a smooth thermal activation heatmap overlay on the original image.\"\"\"\n365:     if cam is None or status == 'PASS':\n366:         return img\n367: \n368:     img_rgb = np.array(img.convert('RGB'))\n369:     cam_uint = np.uint8(np.clip(cam * 255, 0, 255))\n370:     heatmap_color = cv2.applyColorMap(cam_uint, cv2.COLORMAP_JET)\n371:     heatmap_color = cv2.cvtColor(heatmap_color, cv2.COLOR_BGR2RGB)\n372: \n373:     blended = cv2.addWeighted(img_rgb, 0.65, heatmap_color, 0.35, 0)\n374:     return Image.fromarray(blended)\n375: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":546,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-19T16:19:45Z","thinking":"Enhancing the bounding box visualization involves adding target HUD brackets to corners and a high-tech label tag. Box thickness will be dynamically adjusted based on bounding box dimensions to maintain visual clarity. The label will clearly display the detected object's type and confidence level.\n\n\nThe default display mode in the application is the \"Clean Industrial View\", which doesn't show bounding boxes directly. Changing the default to \"Bounding Box\" (or making it the first option) will make the bounding boxes immediately visible to users, addressing the reported issue. This change necessitates modifying the display mode options in the application's configuration. This will enable immediate bounding box visualization, with options to switch to other visualizations such as Grad-CAM heatmap or the raw image.\n\n\nDefect localization utilizes Grad-CAM, followed by a fallback to high-precision contour and gradient analysis when Grad-CAM fails to identify defects. The fallback mechanism ensures bounding box generation even in challenging cases by leveraging edge magnitude and contrast anomaly detection. Dataset loading now supports diverse file types and handles large CSVs efficiently through chunking or sampling.\n\n\nStation column identification will be expanded to include all known aliases to increase robustness across simulation models. Demand resolution will prioritize explicit 'Demand' columns, falling back to deriving it from throughput when necessary to avoid `None` returns. Similarly, total parts will be identified from all known alias columns like \"Total parts\" and \"Entities Out\". Throughput gap and parts-per-hour calculations will be made more robust with these improvements.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"python -c \\\"\\nimport pandas as pd\\nfrom utils.constants import STATION_COLS, DEMAND_COLS, PARTS_COLS\\n\\nprint('Constants imported successfully')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\win-10\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\neurax_app\"","IsDaemon":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking constants import\"","toolSummary":"\"Check constants import\""}}]}
